              "text": "اتارنا — utārnā — \"to take down; to drop off\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "قلی نے ڈبے سے ہمارا سامان اتارا۔ qulī ne ḍabbe se hamārā sāmān utārā. The porter took our luggage down from the carriage."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with نے (he or she …): اس نے صندوق اتارا, us ne sandūq utārā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اتارنا (utārnā) is inherited: CDIAL lists Hindi utārnā, \"to take across, to make descend\", under Sanskrit úttarati and its causative uttārayati (CDIAL 1770). It is the causing partner of اترنا, \"to get off\"."
            }
          ]
        },
